# =============================================================================
# .gitignore for LaTeX (ABNTeX2) projects
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Goal: ignore INTERMEDIATE build artifacts (regenerated on every compile),
#       but KEEP the FINAL artifact (the .pdf) under version control.
#
# Think of it like a compiled language: we commit the source (.tex, .bib,
# images, .cls) and the final "binary" (.pdf), but not the object files.
#
# NOTE: in .gitignore each line is a single pattern. Comments (#) must be on
# their own line -- there are no trailing/inline comments.
# =============================================================================

# --- Core auxiliary files (structure, labels, page layout) -------------------
# .aux  = cross-references, \label/\ref, \cite bookkeeping
# .log  = full compiler log
# .out  = hyperref bookmarks/outline
# .toc/.lof/.lot = table of contents / list of figures / list of tables
# .fls/.fdb_latexmk = latexmk file list and build database
# .synctex.gz/.pdfsync = editor <-> pdf position sync
*.aux
*.log
*.out
*.toc
*.lof
*.lot
*.fls
*.fdb_latexmk
*.synctex.gz
*.synctex(busy)
*.pdfsync

# --- Intermediate output formats ---------------------------------------------
# .dvi/.xdv = pre-PDF output; *-converted-to.* = images auto-converted
*.dvi
*.xdv
*-converted-to.*

# --- Bibliography (BibTeX / Biber) -------------------------------------------
# .bbl = formatted bibliography, .blg = its log, rest = biblatex/biber files
*.bbl
*.blg
*.bcf
*.run.xml
*-blx.aux
*-blx.bib

# --- Index (makeindex) -------------------------------------------------------
*.idx
*.ind
*.ilg
*.ist

# --- Nomenclature / list of symbols (nomencl, used by ABNTeX2) ---------------
*.nlo
*.nls
*.nlg

# --- Glossaries / acronyms (glossaries package) ------------------------------
*.acn
*.acr
*.alg
*.glg
*.glo
*.gls
*.glsdefs
*.slg
*.slo
*.sls

# --- Miscellaneous package leftovers -----------------------------------------
# .brf = hyperref backrefs, .tdo = todonotes, .xdy = xindy, .bak = editor backup
*.brf
*.tdo
*.xdy
*.bak

# --- Overleaf-specific leftovers ---------------------------------------------
# .pdfxref = Overleaf's PDF cross-reference cache (uncompressed/compressed
# object offsets); regenerated on every Overleaf compile.
*.pdfxref

# --- Temporary / scratch files -----------------------------------------------
# A local 'temp' directory for scratch files that must never be committed.
/temp/

# --- Editor / IDE config -----------------------------------------------------
# Local Emacs project config kept out of version control
ides/emacs/.emacs-revinfor/

# =============================================================================
# FINAL PDF: by default every .pdf is ignored (regenerable artifact). The
# exception below re-includes the generated article PDFs (main-<flavor>-<engine>.pdf,
# e.g. main-overleaf-pdf.pdf) so they ARE version-controlled, while any OTHER
# .pdf (reference material, etc.) stays ignored.
#
# How the two lines work together: git applies patterns top-to-bottom, and a
# later "!" (negation) re-includes files matched by an earlier rule. So keep
# "!main*.pdf" AFTER "*.pdf". (Negation cannot re-include a file inside an
# ignored directory, but here the article folders are not ignored, so it works.)
# =============================================================================
*.pdf
!main*.pdf
